  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_ARTIFACT` | The target spec / task does not exist |
    | `H_PARENT_SPEC_MISSING` | A task's parent spec is missing — cannot critique a task without its spec |
    | `H_DISPATCH_FAILED` | The sensor subagent failed to dispatch twice — surface to the operator, do not loop silently |
    | `H_MAX_ROUNDS` | Cap of 5 rounds hit and still not CLEAN — escalate to the operator (`AX_CAP_5`) |
    | `H_GOAL_BLOCKED` | `GOAL` findings block the round and the operator is unavailable to answer — stop, report the pending question block |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_RESOLVE">
      <Goal>Resolve the target.</Goal>
      <Action>Spec / task / batch (spec + its tasks — critiqued in DAG layers, parallel within a layer, per `AX_TASK_PARALLEL`). Missing → `H_NO_ARTIFACT`.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_0B_PREFLIGHT">
      <Goal>Clear the FLOW_VERSION/READINESS preflight gate before dispatching the sensor.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Use `FLOW_VERSION`, `READINESS`, and `GATE_QUEUE` from the already-gathered `sdd-state`
        snapshot; do not enter task lifecycle merely to clear this gate. Size the gate to this request's own blast radius
        (`AX_PREFLIGHT_BLAST_RADIUS_SCOPED`).

        {{> "contract/process/readiness-preflight-gate"}}
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_DISPATCH">
      <Goal>Dispatch the isolated sensor.</Goal>
      <Action>One fresh subagent, on a worker-tier model — never stronger than the author's model (`AX_CRITIC_MODEL_TIER`): read `ai/directives/sdd-v2/critic-protocol.directive.xml` + the artifact + parent spec only (`AX_ISOLATION_SIGNAL`). Tell the sensor which round this is — `Round: <N>` in the dispatch — so it reads the artifact's `## Critic Rounds` history with the right expectation (`AX_SCRATCH_LOG`). Emit a round progress line (`ORCHESTRATOR_PROGRESS_FORMAT`).</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_EVALUATE">
      <Goal>Weigh findings against full project context.</Goal>
      <Action>Split by addressee (`AX_FINDING_ADDRESSEE`): `MECHANICAL` — accept by default (`AX_DEFAULT_ACCEPT`); `GOAL` — queue for STEP_3B, keep the touched sections intact (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`). The sensor's `GOAL` tag is a floor, not a ceiling: downgrading it to `MECHANICAL` is the operator's call alone (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`) — an orchestrator read that leans mechanical carries into STEP_3B as one more question, never a private reclassification. A rejection cites a specific file / section that resolves the concern (`AX_REJECTION_REASON`). Sensor confusion the full context resolves = an artifact bug — clarify by edit (`AX_CONFUSION_BUG`); confusion the project cannot answer = `GOAL`. Also carry each finding's severity (`AX_SEVERITY`) forward — STEP_3B gates on it. A finding that removes or weakens a quality gate is `GOAL` by definition, never a private `MECHANICAL` call (`AX_FINDING_ADDRESSEE`) — e.g. a sensor surfacing that pre-commit's staged-file `tsc` run cannot also be whole-project: which way to resolve that contradiction is the operator's call, not the orchestrator's, and the answer becomes its own Decision Log entry (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`).

      Convergence brake from round 3 on: a NEW finding (not already carried in a prior `## Critic Rounds` entry) advances to STEP_3 / STEP_3B only if `CRITICAL`, or a regression — a defect a prior round's own edit introduced. A new `MINOR` / `MAJOR` finding that is neither stays out of this cycle's edit set — record it in this round's entry under `Out of cycle:` and carry it into the STEP_5 report as its own list, never silently dropped (AUTHORING.md §9 — a stop needs a named outlet, not a bare refusal).</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2B_RECONCILE">
      <Goal>Walk the graph from the artifact to the portal; reconcile every entity the WHOLE artifact introduces, not only this round's findings. (mechanical → tool)</Goal>
      <Action>Run `npx gennady sdd-orient <artifact-path>` ONCE against the critiqued artifact itself — one hop from the artifact to its portal, its declared-dependency neighbours, and its consumers; this is the ORCHESTRATOR's own step, on full project context, not a widening of the sensor's bounded read (`AX_ISOLATION_SIGNAL` still governs STEP_1_DISPATCH — the sensor stays isolated). The sweep is proactive over EVERY entity/contract/mechanism the artifact introduces, never narrowed to only the entities this round's findings happen to name — a duplicate the sensor never flagged is still a duplicate. For each: reuse > extend > justify > escalate (`AX_REUSE_FIRST`); "justify" requires the specific neighbour invariant/requirement ID the existing mechanism could not satisfy, recorded as its own Decision Log entry (`AX_PARALLEL_MECHANISM_REQUIRES_JUSTIFICATION`, `AX_DECISION_LOG_REQUIRED`). Two outcomes route to `GOAL`, never a silent `MECHANICAL` fix: (1) the artifact duplicates a mechanism the `sdd-orient` extract already names on a neighbour, (2) the artifact's introduced entity conflicts with a neighbour requirement the extract surfaces. Do not let the critique invent a duplicate of an existing entity.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_EDIT">
      <Goal>Apply the round's `MECHANICAL` edits.</Goal>
      <Action>Edit only what a finding requires (`AX_SURGICAL`); I apply the edits — the sensor never does (`AX_OWNER`). Apply every `MECHANICAL` finding directly, regardless of severity (`AX_DEFAULT_ACCEPT`) — a `CRITICAL` / `MAJOR` mechanical finding gets fixed now, confirmed with the operator next at STEP_3B, not gated before the fix. Leave `GOAL`-tagged sections untouched — their edit waits for the operator's answer at STEP_3B. The round's edits are recorded once, together, at STEP_3C — not here.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3B_ROUND_CHECKPOINT">
      <Goal>One batch Ask per round for every operator-owned item (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Resolve every `GOAL` finding against accepted operator decisions and the Decision Log first.
        An established answer is applied with its source cited; a low-risk default that preserves
        product intent is recorded and applied without Ask. Only a genuinely new product fork enters
        the batch, and its question names the new consequence that reopened it. Build ONE
        `AskUserQuestion` batch (`QUESTION_FORMAT` batching rule — independent questions ride
        together) carrying, when present: (a) every remaining new `GOAL` fork from STEP_2 or STEP_2B as its own question,
        including any orchestrator disagreement with a sensor's `GOAL` tag («critic tagged GOAL, I read
        this as mechanical because …») — the tag stands until this answer says otherwise; (b) IF this
        round carried any `CRITICAL` / `MAJOR` finding (mechanical or goal), one confirm block: «critic
        found N problems this round, fixed as follows: <one line per fix> — confirm, or correct?».
        Neither (a) nor (b) applies (the round was `MINOR` / `INFO` only, or carried zero findings) →
        skip the Ask, go straight to STEP_3C (`AX_DEFAULT_ACCEPT`). WAIT for the answer
        before touching any `GOAL`-tagged section. Apply `GOAL` edits exactly as answered, and any
        correction the operator makes to a confirmed fix — recorded together at STEP_3C, not here.
        When the answered `GOAL` finding weakened or removed a quality gate, additionally write the
        operator's decision as its own Decision Log entry (`AX_GOAL_OWNER_GATE`). Operator unreachable
        while `GOAL` findings block → `H_GOAL_BLOCKED`.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3C_RECORD_ROUND">
      <Goal>Append this round's memory to the artifact (`AX_SCRATCH_LOG`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Append ONE entry to `## Critic Rounds` in the artifact — create the section (at the end of the
        artifact) the first round that needs it; never rewrite a prior entry, this block is append-only:

        ```
        ### Round <N> — <YYYY-MM-DD>
        - Verdict: <CLEAN|NEEDS_WORK|CRITICAL>
        - Accepted: <count> — <list>
        - Rejected: <count> — "<finding>" → <reason>
        - Reconcile: <entity → REUSE <target> | EXTEND <target> | JUSTIFY <rationale> | ESCALATE>
        - Changes: <list>
        - Out of cycle: <new MINOR/MAJOR findings the round-3+ brake deferred, or "none">
        ```

        `Accepted` covers both the `MECHANICAL` edits applied at STEP_3 and the `GOAL` edits applied at
        STEP_3B after the operator's answer. `Rejected` carries the exact reason per `AX_REJECTION_REASON`
        — a later round, or a later session picking this up fresh, reads this entry before re-raising the
        same ground. Even on a `CLEAN` round this entry is appended before STEP_5 deletes the whole block
        — the verdict line is what STEP_5 quotes.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_DECIDE">
      <Goal>Loop or stop.</Goal>
      <Action>Edits applied this round (STEP_3 or STEP_3B) → re-dispatch (`AX_RE_DISPATCH` — mandatory, no self-made exception for a fix judged trivial). Zero edits → stop (`AX_STOP_NO_EDITS`). Cap 5 (`AX_CAP_5`) → `H_MAX_ROUNDS`.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_FINALIZE">
      <Goal>Finalize.</Goal>
      <Action>On CLEAN: delete the `## Critic Rounds` scratch; the artifact is clean with improvements integrated. Report the final verdict (CLEAN | NEEDS_WORK | CRITICAL) with a one-line-per-round summary of what changed, plus — when any round recorded an `Out of cycle` list — a merged `Out of cycle` section collecting every deferred finding across rounds, so nothing the brake held back is silently lost. The reported verdict MUST be the literal verdict text of the LAST sensor dispatch actually run (`AX_RE_DISPATCH`), shown as a direct quote, never a paraphrase and never an earlier round's verdict presented as current. A structural problem the critique cannot resolve by a surgical edit → escalate to the operator, do not loop.</Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

